  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Electrifying the Addis#Djibouti Corridor: Pilot High-Power Charging and Skills Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopia presents strong structural conditions for freight electrification, including a near-100% renewable electricity grid, very low electricity tariffs, supportive national e-mobility policy direction, and concentrated freight demand along the Addis#Djibouti co rridor.  Despite this high potential, no freight-grade high-power charging infrastructure exists along the corridor and no standardized technical or operating model has been established.  UNIDO has conducted stakeholder mapping and is facilitating discussions between:  Alpitronic (European high-power DC charging manufacturer)  Ethio Telecom (national infrastructure operator)  Both actors have expressed interest in exploring pilot deployment of 2#3 high-power charging hubs.  UNIDO is also engaging with the European Union Delegation (EUD) in Ethiopia to explore positioning under the EU Global Gateway strategy.  This initiative is being advanced through collaboration between:  Skills Development, Entrepreneurship and Fair Production (IET/PST/SEF)  Sustainable Energy and Just Transitions (TCS/ECA/JET)  The PA is requested to conduct the technical, financial, institutional and skills-related feasibility work required to develop a donor-ready Project Document for pilot deployment and blended finance structuring.</narrative>
  </description>
